INSERT INTO "task_definition" ("task_id","schema_version","title","objective","source_path","status_detail","explicit_activation_required","intake_path","archive_path","archive_sha256","documentation_path") VALUES ('migration.v2.calculators',3,'V2 calculator contracts package','Introduce shared plane-wave simulation-specification contracts plus project-facing calculator-specific SimulationTask, Simulation, immutable input/output, executable, process, backend-binding, and executor-protocol contracts.','tasks/software/migration.v2.calculators.json','The human response `commit and push`, answering the request to authorize parent acceptance and administrative closeout including the validated commit and push, accepts this bounded parent result and authorizes its managed closeout. The earlier human response `yes this is selected` selected aggregate verification and parent closeout preparation. The subsequent human response `yes` to `Do you want the remaining tutorial consumer migrated and _dft retired before closing the parent?` authorizes the completed bounded retirement. The four closed human-accepted child results compose under the accepted ownership split: backend-neutral contracts in calculators.dft.pw and QE-specific contracts in integration.quantum_espresso. The retained silicon tutorial now constructs existing Workflow replay and analysis inputs directly; calculators/_dft.py and its two obsolete direct test modules are removed without relocation or compatibility aliases. Retained observations, native inputs, expected report bytes, supported plane-wave and QE contracts, and historical child acceptance records are unchanged. Ten probe-only evidence owners and the old importability claim retire; SV-CALCULATOR-VERIFY-008 establishes absence, and the tutorial retains SV-RETAINED-SILICON-BAND-PROBE-001 under one Test owner with new dependency evidence 002. Verification reports 27 focused passed cases and 3718 full-suite passed cases with three existing unavailable-external-QEXSD skips, full Ruff lint and formatting, complete mypy including the migrated example, Python evidence conformance, Sphinx warnings-as-errors, Harness validation, synchronized projection integrity, and diff checks. No blocking finding remains in the writer''s bounded reconciliation; no independent reviewer was delegated. Private Workflow replay and analysis remain separately owned and unsupported as public APIs. This result establishes bounded software verification only, not new numerical verification, scientific validation, uncertainty quantification, backend equivalence, or scientific acceptance. Managed closeout clears the selection and requires one validated commit, its configured-upstream push, and remote-identity verification. Dependency changes, protected execution, publication, release, and successor activation remain unauthorized.',1,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL);
INSERT INTO "task_definition" ("task_id","schema_version","title","objective","source_path","status_detail","explicit_activation_required","intake_path","archive_path","archive_sha256","documentation_path") VALUES ('migration.v2.calculators.contract-verification',3,'V2 calculator contract verification','Verify calculator contract composition, dependency direction, exact inputs/outputs, and protocol behavior.','tasks/software/migration.v2.calculators.contract-verification.json','The human response `human acceptance and closeout authorized` explicitly authorizes managed administrative closeout and constitutes final human acceptance of the calculator contract-verification result activated by the earlier response `continue and use adverserial analysis`. The accepted result preserves the backend-neutral `PlaneWaveCalculator` protocol, verifies strict generic integration-owned input/output composition, and closes `PlaneWaveBackendCompilationFailure` with one exact failure outcome for each failure code plus exhaustive rejection of all 12 contradictory pairs. The private `calculators._dft` architecture probe remains importable only through its private path because the maintained silicon-bands tutorial still consumes it; its records and two test modules were migrated to strict callable and test-owner conformance without promoting that probe to a supported package export. Package topology has one artifact evidence owner without duplicated containment assertions. Eight calculator verification modules contain 21 unique evidence owners and report 35 passed cases; the complete configured suite reports 3727 passed with 3 skipped environment-dependent external-QEXSD cases. Full Ruff lint and formatting, complete mypy, Python evidence conformance, Sphinx warnings-as-errors, Harness validation, synchronized projection integrity, and diff checks passed. Two adversarial read-only reviews identified six deterministic findings in total; all were corrected, and reviewer agreement itself provides no acceptance. This accepted result establishes bounded software verification only; it establishes no dependency change, protected or scientific execution, numerical verification, scientific validation, uncertainty quantification, scientific acceptance, publication, release, or automatic successor activation.',1,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL);
INSERT INTO "task_definition" ("task_id","schema_version","title","objective","source_path","status_detail","explicit_activation_required","intake_path","archive_path","archive_sha256","documentation_path") VALUES ('migration.v2.calculators.plane-wave-study-contracts',3,'V2 plane-wave QoI and parameter-study contracts','Define and prove the smallest backend-neutral, QoI-driven plane-wave parameter-study contract before stabilizing Quantum ESPRESSO-specific calculator contracts.','tasks/software/migration.v2.calculators.plane-wave-study-contracts.json','The human response `administrative closeout` explicitly authorized administrative closeout and constitutes final human acceptance of this bounded architecture and private-software stabilization task. The accepted result defines calculator-neutral QoI observation requirements, immutable parameter-study revisions, typed plane-wave specifications and backend supplements, effect-free compilation into exact run-scoped Task-instance plans and dependencies, complete-binding reuse, and a nominal ParameterStudyRefiner ABC with one deterministic finite-sequence implementation and independently validated immutable successor state. Independent review findings concerning exact Task plans, full-binding reuse equality, QoI observation coverage, malformed predecessor state, successor-state identity reuse, result vocabularies, request/compiler correlation, evidence claims, and provisional status wording were corrected. Maintained tests use one primary owner per module, with package-export smoke evidence separately artifact-owned. Verification passed for 3,590 repository tests with three unavailable external QE artifact tests skipped, targeted Ruff and strict mypy, Python evidence conformance for seven class-owned modules and one artifact-owned module, Sphinx warnings-as-errors, Harness validation, synchronized projection integrity, and diff checks. Human acceptance applies only to this bounded architecture and private synthetic software probe; no calculator execution, stable public API, dependency change, production parameter selection, physical convergence, scientific validation or acceptance, uncertainty quantification, backend equivalence, publication, release, or automatic successor activation is claimed. The Quantum ESPRESSO successor remains inactive.',1,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL);
INSERT INTO "task_definition" ("task_id","schema_version","title","objective","source_path","status_detail","explicit_activation_required","intake_path","archive_path","archive_sha256","documentation_path") VALUES ('migration.v2.calculators.quantum-espresso-contracts',3,'V2 Quantum ESPRESSO calculator contracts','Coordinate the approved bounded child tasks that decide, implement, bind, and verify project-facing QE SimulationTask, Simulation, immutable input/output, and executor protocol contracts.','tasks/software/migration.v2.calculators.quantum-espresso-contracts.json','The human response `parent administrative closeout authorized` explicitly authorizes administrative closeout and constitutes final human acceptance of the completed parent containment result. The accepted parent records the closed human-accepted boundary-decision, task-contracts, simulation-and-executor-bindings, and contract-verification children. Aggregate verification included one deterministic stale-DOS documentation correction and a fresh independent read-only review with no remaining material finding. No new implementation, dependency change, protected execution, numerical verification, scientific validation, release, publication, or automatic succession is claimed or authorized, and no successor is active.',1,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL);
INSERT INTO "task_definition" ("task_id","schema_version","title","objective","source_path","status_detail","explicit_activation_required","intake_path","archive_path","archive_sha256","documentation_path") VALUES ('migration.v2.calculators.quantum-espresso-contracts.boundary-decision',3,'Decide the V2 Quantum ESPRESSO task-contract boundary','Resolve the exact public operation taxonomy, class names, and ownership boundary for project-facing Quantum ESPRESSO SimulationTask and Simulation contracts.','tasks/software/migration.v2.calculators.quantum-espresso-contracts.boundary-decision.json','The human response `authorized` explicitly authorizes administrative closeout and constitutes final human acceptance of the selected Option B architecture decision. The accepted decision establishes operation-specific QuantumEspressoScfTask, QuantumEspressoNscfTask, QuantumEspressoBandPathTask, and QuantumEspressoBandsExtractionTask contracts under integration.quantum_espresso; retains QuantumEspressoPwResult and QuantumEspressoBandsResult as executable-oriented mechanical evidence; and defers DOS until its executable and result boundary exists. The decision document, resolved checkpoint, synchronized architecture pages, checkpoint validation, Sphinx warnings-as-errors build, Harness validation, and projection integrity pass. No implementation, protected execution, scientific acceptance, dependency change, publication, release, or automatic successor activation is accepted or authorized, and no successor is active.',1,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL);
